-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yakecen-Sings</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=805382#post805382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> *Runs in wild, excited circles*</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, right? I mean, I've seen a few unofficial fan-made concepts, but I'm looking forward to what those Rank glyphs will be like.<br /> I wonder if Richard Thomas designed them as he did with the other glyphs, or if they're made in the same style?<br /> <br /> I'll see if I can get any answers from the BNS folks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T03:48:42-08:00","id":805959,"title":"","content":"I have a question for you folks. I love Werewolf the Apocalypse, but as a LARP it horribly stretches my suspension of disbelief. It's the kind of game that's supposed to have a giant special effects budget, and the theatre of the mind is much better suited to that then the LARP environment.<br /> <br /> How does the MET Werewolf work? How does it cope with the physicallity and freakishness of Werewolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T06:26:36-08:00","id":806025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=805959#post805959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question for you folks. I love Werewolf the Apocalypse, but as a LARP it horribly stretches my suspension of disbelief. It's the kind of game that's supposed to have a giant special effects budget, and the theatre of the mind is much better suited to that then the LARP environment.<br /> <br /> How does the MET Werewolf work? How does it cope with the physicallity and freakishness of Werewolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>It actually works best of them all. Werewolf has a great setting for LARP where all the PCs are hypothetically on the same side, but they have very strong differences of opinion on how to get it done. As for special effects, you'd be surprised how far a pair of kneepads and growling will get you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T09:55:37-08:00","id":806184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=805959#post805959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...) and the theatre of the mind is much better suited to that then the LARP environment.</div> </div> </div> </div> The simple answer, and I mean this without snarkiness, is that it isn't one or the other; you bring the mind's eye into the LARP and it really does a great deal of the work. Imagination rules in a LARP, and you have to be willing to let yourself get caught up in the inertia of it. For some types of people, this is a lot more difficult - nothing wrong with that, it's just how their brains are wired, and they feed off of visual cues more than imaginary ones - but not impossible. In cases like that it seems like a LARP that has a greater dedication to costuming really helps bridge it.<br /> <br /> In my experience, Werewolf invites a lot more storytelling because a lot more has to be imagination-spun, from not just the ST but each player. It makes it more crucial that you have a good, involved ST - moreso than a setting where you get more of the feedback visually, say maybe Vampire or Hunter - who can not just paint these scenes, but yarn you into them and stir your feelings. When the mind in interested and invested in something, it is naturally more inclined to be involved and fill in blanks.<br /> <br /> After a strong Storyteller, you need to be willing to tap into your inner child just enough to not worry about how silly it might look when you start menacing someone with your clawed hand, curling your lip and snarling at them, with your other hand making a &quot;C&quot; (this is what we've used in our LARPs to indicate Crinos form) but once you get into the stride of it, it doesn't really matter. Everything else falls away, and your mind learns to read these posture cues and again fill in the blanks. But you, as a player, have to be willing to relax your grip on pride and just go for it with confidence, and weave for yourself a solid head space of your character. So a lot of the responsibility is on the individual player, I feel, to not just participate but contribute to the immersion, and that has a meta way of tying into the themes of community in the setting as a whole. Special effects are then largely just supplied by the mind's eye.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T10:00:33-08:00","id":806186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=805959#post805959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question for you folks. I love Werewolf the Apocalypse, but as a LARP it horribly stretches my suspension of disbelief. It's the kind of game that's supposed to have a giant special effects budget, and the theatre of the mind is much better suited to that then the LARP environment.<br /> <br /> How does the MET Werewolf work? How does it cope with the physicallity and freakishness of Werewolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well at a distance a werewolf larp looks like a bunch of people playing rock paper scissors intermixed with the thriller dance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T15:37:36-08:00","id":806524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=805959#post805959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question for you folks. I love Werewolf the Apocalypse, but as a LARP it horribly stretches my suspension of disbelief. It's the kind of game that's supposed to have a giant special effects budget, and the theatre of the mind is much better suited to that then the LARP environment.<br /> <br /> How does the MET Werewolf work? How does it cope with the physicallity and freakishness of Werewolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>Parlor LARPs, to me, are more an extension of tabletop because beyond some costuming and moving around, the &quot;action&quot; takes place in your mind.<br /> Friends of mine have been working on some foam-combat-style LARP rules for W:tA, which I think would be much more beneficial to a W:tA LARP game than MET. But if you understand that the scenes are narrated just like TT (basically it breaks down into TT with Rock/Paper/Scissors), then the expectation isn't that it's going to feel like a frenzied scene OOC, but you'll have to use your imagination like TT. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T19:33:05-08:00","id":806682,"title":"","content":"I wonder if BNS is any less racist than they were when they did MET V20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T05:02:41-08:00","id":806917,"title":"","content":"Don't take my comment as critique of the Werewolf LARP. It's just that I've never had an opportunity to participate in one, and this feeling is probably the biggest problem that I have with pitching in for something like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T07:23:58-08:00","id":806995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=806682#post806682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if BNS is any less racist than they were when they did MET V20.</div> </div> </div> </div>They released a Gamma Slice that includes all of the Tribes that are highly correlated with race, and it doesn't seem worse than other WW products. What I'm waiting for before backing is more setting info, since what they have released suggests that the Western Concordiat has broken up, and the Coggies, Glass Walkers, Shadow Lords, and Uktena have all Fallen to the Weaver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T10:18:04-08:00","id":807122,"title":"","content":"I suspect that the setting may change now that Paradox is involved, and will probably direct it more towards their One World of Darkness setting.<br /> <br /> That being said, I didn't necessarily feel that the other Tribes had fallen to the Weaver, but the Glass Walkers certainly seemed to be reveling in their successes, and most Tribes seemed much more... stereotypes as their Tribes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T16:51:00-08:00","id":807424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=807122#post807122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect that the setting may change now that Paradox is involved, and will probably direct it more towards their One World of Darkness setting.<br /> <br /> That being said, I didn't necessarily feel that the other Tribes had fallen to the Weaver, but the Glass Walkers certainly seemed to be reveling in their successes, and most Tribes seemed much more... stereotypes as their Tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really understand how else to explain the change from Revised's &quot;Maybe The Weaver is just as bad as the Wyrm, guys&quot; to &quot;Let's ally with The Weaver against the Wyrm&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T17:55:23-08:00","id":807469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=806995#post806995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They released a Gamma Slice that includes all of the Tribes that are highly correlated with race, and it doesn't seem worse than other WW products.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could very possibly be damning with faint praise, even in comparison to modern works. For instance, Forsaken and its deal with making all of the Japanese Uratha descended from Ainu (which can also qualify as a raw numbers demography fail).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What I'm waiting for before backing is more setting info, since what they have released suggests that the Western Concordiat has broken up, and the Coggies, Glass Walkers, Shadow Lords, and Uktena have all Fallen to the Weaver. </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XZxzJGgox_E\" data-code=\"XZxzJGgox_E\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/XZxzJGgox_E/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T19:25:52-08:00","id":807515,"title":"","content":"This weekend I'll be at Midwinter Gaming Convention in Milwaukee, Wisconsin where BNS will be doing their &quot;<a href=\"http://www.bynightstudios.com/midwinter-gaming-convention-rage-retribution-remix/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage and Retribution Remix</a>&quot; event, so maybe it'll be a good time to corner them and ask some of the questions too.<br /> Like I said before, I'm curious how much of the setting/story will change now that Paradox Interactive is more involved in the project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T20:09:37-08:00","id":807546,"title":"","content":"So I skimmed the book, and am I reading things wrong or does it seem like the majority of the tribes seem to not have a problem with their Metis? I got that feeling from the Revised tribe books as well where it seemed to be more &quot;blame the parents, not the child&quot; from the bulk of those books (with a few exceptions, Fianna, Red Talon, and Silver Fang), while the LARP book seems to more point to have a similar feel (all the tribes but the Fianna, Red Talons, Shadow Lords, Silver Fangs, and maybe the Uktena since it says they are feared). I'd like to see what other people think or if I am just reading into things. I hope I'm wrong, or it takes away from the whole concept that the Metis are treated poorly if the other 7 tribes don't seem to have much of an issue with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-12T20:18:55-08:00","id":807550,"title":"","content":"Also, thoughts on male non-metis Black Furies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T00:55:40-08:00","id":807697,"title":"","content":"And here i thought my main problem with this is going to be the suspension of disbelief :P<br /> Where can we find a list or writeup of these setting changes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T05:18:19-08:00","id":807793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=807550#post807550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, thoughts on male non-metis Black Furies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda missing the point of the tribe,imho. I can understand admitting transwomen, but straight up men? Also, there might be a rule where biting a kin makes a garou. Haven't checked yet, but I heard that from a pretty reliable source.<br /> <br /> As for metis treatment, its not really too different from the revisited/20th ed. Only thing is that Get of Fenris seem far more hostile towards them than they were in revised ed. Most tribes really only focus on usefulness of them in the end.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, my pet peeve, garou holding jobs. Now Ahroun seem to somehow be in the military a lot, with their rage 5 XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 01-13-2016, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T06:00:13-08:00","id":807808,"title":"","content":"I'd like a list of changes or contradictions, too.<br /> <br /> I just browsed through the Gamma Slice and rules to the Curse aren't in there. But I laid eyes upon the Fianna tribal weakness. Dots in Retainers, Contacts and Allies return only half as fast as usual and effects of the loss of loved ones is doubled in regards to Harano. All due to a Fae Curse places upon the Arg Righ and by extension all Fianna around the year 2000. All their Fae friendships now on ice.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if I need changes to the setting like that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T06:14:37-08:00","id":807817,"title":"","content":"Okay, just having read a little more:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Umbral Storms</b><br /> The Umbral Storms have forever altered how the Garou interact with the Umbra and travel through its realms. Umbra realms that were once familiar and safe are now dangerous and chaotic. Traveling the Umbra is arduous at best and deadly if you are unlucky. Only the bawn of a caern or shard caern provides sanctuary from the storms, allowing the Garou to explore the Umbra without risk.<br /> These wicked spiritual storms can cause terrible damage including:<br /> \u2022 Disrupting the few remaining Moon Bridges<br /> \u2022 Rending the Gauntlet, creating a periphery zone that can release spirits, banes, and devastation upon the material realm<br /> \u2022 Creating Wyrm-Holes, allowing banes to spread Wyrm-Taint into Wyld lands<br /> \u2022 Spread nightmares and madness to human populations in the Material Realm<br /> \u2022 Disrupting travel in the Umbra<br /> \u2022 Carrying enemy spirits, banes, and other creatures into protected realms, or even the bawn of a caern </div> </div> </div>Not sure how much of the game they describe there is the WtA I use to play.<br /> Actually, I was thinking it kind of is &quot;nWoD&quot;-like or even Monte Cook's WoD-like to have humans terrorized by nightmares and spirits interacting with the world more often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T06:53:57-08:00","id":807839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=807817#post807817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, just having read a little more:<br /> <br /> Not sure how much of the game they describe there is the WtA I use to play.<br /> Actually, I was thinking it kind of is &quot;nWoD&quot;-like or even Monte Cook's WoD-like to have humans terrorized by nightmares and spirits interacting with the world more often.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very Monte Cook. Thoughts on &quot;Shard Caerns&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T07:20:58-08:00","id":807856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=807839#post807839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very Monte Cook. Thoughts on &quot;Shard Caerns&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>They seem interesting, especially that they are mobile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T07:55:15-08:00","id":807881,"title":"","content":"Sure, it is interesting, but a world where the Garou Nation has had setbacks in a way that most caerns are destroyed and alliances with the fera are more common and shard caerns exist and what not... is it still W:tA or is it Werewolf: Age of Apocalypse ?<br /> <br /> The term &quot;Age of Apocalypse&quot; surely is used frequent in the gamma slice and since Martin co-operated closely with BNS, we might see a lot of what any 4th edition of a World of Darkness game might look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T10:16:00-08:00","id":807993,"title":"","content":"I don't mind some changes, the Concordat of Stars seems like a cool idea. Something I've been thinking myself, though not with Weaver support. And the more traditional garou opposing it sounds neat.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I do think there are a bit too many changes. Especially with the &quot;we should ally with Weaver&quot; aspect, to match our modern social media/technology. I don't like that, you can have the dislike for Weaver creations without making garou luddites. The 20th ed book is pretty good example of of that.<br /> <br /> That, and the Furies accepting males and most of the CoG text aren't bad, but they ring hollow. You can be accepting without making it such a major point.<br /> <br /> Then the Umbral storm. Didn't we have similar in Mage? Wasn't that thing pretty -hated-?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T13:34:00-08:00","id":808187,"title":"","content":"The avatar storm was controversial, but the Umbra storm is kind of different - I'd guess. It seems as a plot device to destroy most caerns in the world, make the penumbra outside of bawns pretty nasty and have Gauntlet weakspots where spirits and banes can torment humans...<br /> <br /> Like I said, it seems the WoD is taking a turn for the worst. Not sure if I like the number of changes, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T13:52:31-08:00","id":808209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=808187#post808187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The avatar storm was controversial, but the Umbra storm is kind of different - I'd guess. It seems as a plot device to destroy most caerns in the world, make the penumbra outside of bawns pretty nasty and have Gauntlet weakspots where spirits and banes can torment humans...<br /> <br /> Like I said, it seems the WoD is taking a turn for the worst. Not sure if I like the number of changes, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's arguably worse than the Avatar Storm, because the Umbra is even more of a part of Werewolf than it is of Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T14:29:38-08:00","id":808233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=808209#post808209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's arguably worse than the Avatar Storm, because the Umbra is even more of a part of Werewolf than it is of Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, plus Umbra is all ready poorly used in some games (though I dunno 'bout LARPs), this will make it even harder to use.<br /> <br /> As I said, I don't mind changing stuff, but this is pretty bad for a game about spirituality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T16:34:32-08:00","id":808307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=807793#post807793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kinda missing the point of the tribe,imho. I can understand admitting transwomen, but straight up men? Also, there might be a rule where biting a kin makes a garou. Haven't checked yet, but I heard that from a pretty reliable source.<br /> EDIT: Also, my pet peeve, garou holding jobs. Now Ahroun seem to somehow be in the military a lot, with their rage 5 XD</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this, this is the big change I have an issue with. <br /> <br /> As for the Metis thing, I brought it up because the books paint the metis out as this 2nd class citizen of the Nation. It's hard for me to take that seriously if the bulk of the tribes don't have an issue with them. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T16:51:16-08:00","id":808315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=808307#post808307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the Metis thing, I brought it up because the books paint the metis out as this 2nd class citizen of the Nation. It's hard for me to take that seriously if the bulk of the tribes don't have an issue with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least 20th ed notes that most tribes are warming up to them a bit. But its just more out of pragmatism for the tribes and the fact that metis are still playable. There has to be reason why a tribe lets a metis join and reach to cliath, after all. Its not really that they don't have issues, its just that all garou are needed, and to some tribes it really isn't worth the trouble to put metis down when they could be doing something useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T17:42:48-08:00","id":808336,"title":"","content":"Corax have a glabro form it looks like now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T17:43:45-08:00","id":808338,"title":"","content":"I post too soon, Hispo equivalent too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T18:00:32-08:00","id":808348,"title":"","content":"Thoughts on having purchase merits to play characters such as Fera? A merit that can still be rejected by the story teller? I don't get the point personally, if a ST is ok with someone playing a rare character (like a Fera) why should that cost freebie points?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T18:06:19-08:00","id":808351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=808348#post808348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts on having purchase merits to play characters such as Fera? A merit that can still be rejected by the story teller? I don't get the point personally, if a ST is ok with someone playing a rare character (like a Fera) why should that cost freebie points?</div> </div> </div> </div>O.o ....o.O<br /> <br /> Uh, anyone LARPing, is this a thing there? Because it sounds very silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T18:47:57-08:00","id":808369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=808338#post808338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I post too soon, Hispo equivalent too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Giving everyone five forms is a change that I could get behind. Not worth it in this case, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T18:50:32-08:00","id":808371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=808351#post808351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> O.o ....o.O<br /> <br /> Uh, anyone LARPing, is this a thing there? Because it sounds very silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it's a thing and yes it's silly and I can say that unabashedly because not only have I larped but I've ran a few too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T20:53:42-08:00","id":808429,"title":"","content":"I get where many of these changes are coming from too.<br /> This is a game book that is being designed with fluff and crunch (setting/story and mechanics) built for large LARP organizations to use, as well as local singular event/clubs too.<br /> They're also looking at what may work in other LARPs, and trying to apply new mechanics that (to them) work better in these settings rather than trying to directly translate what's in the books.<br /> <br /> I actually like the fracturing of the Tribes, and amping up their uniqueness. Playing a Metis in a LARP doesn't necessarily come with much penalty considering the way a lot of LARPs are played, so why punish players for playing such characters? Sure the Mules are looked down upon as representations of breaking the Litany and being sterile, but warriors that are sterile due to their fighting in the battles aren't looked down upon and are instead given Renown for their Battle Scars. <br /> <br /> Speaking of Renown, the &quot;Spend Renown&quot; system is something I'm still trying to wrap my head around too. You spend your Renown on Gifts and stuff, rather than having some grand number that makes up your Rank. I've got to see this played out before I really can comment on its usage though.<br /> <br /> However, again, I want to say that it's POSSIBLE that all of the setting stuff could be changed with Paradox Interactive's involvement, and many of the mechanics could still be changed with reworking the system from the Gamma Version playtests going on. So NONE of it is written in stone yet.<br /> <br /> Also, page #398 of the <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/169846/Minds-Eye-Theatre-Werewolf-The-Apocalypse-Gamma-Slice-Playtest-Rules\" target=\"_blank\">Gamma Slice</a> (<a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/169846/Minds-Eye-Theatre-Werewolf-The-Apocalypse-Gamma-Slice-Playtest-Rules\" target=\"_blank\">free download on DriveThruRPG</a>) has a Feedback Form, but PLEASE read through the book, or try out the mechanics before responding. Be constructive too, not just destructive! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T23:59:14-08:00","id":808495,"title":"","content":"At the December convention in Germany Martin Ericsson, the new Head Storyteller at White Wolf (the Paradox Incarnation), stated, that he collaborated closely on MET:Werewolf and that it has some elements that show where he wants the World of Darkness to head to.<br /> <br /> Having the Garou Nation kind of defunct, most caerns destroyed and shard caerns and hostile Umbra and random places where the Gauntlet is weak as story hooks all seem to be changes to the setting of Werewolf and the World of Darkness as a whole that imo didn't happen without his consent. Martin said he wanted the World of Darkness to evolve and therefore we can assume more changes are coming - to Vampire too.<br /> <br /> OPPs &quot;Nostalgia Line&quot; (aka the x20 books and their supplements) won't be affected, as far as I heard. But I've no idea how it will go on after the last x20's have been released. At some point Martin will have designed Vampire IV and then books to this setting will be all the new books we get.<br /> <br /> But what I've read from the Gamma slice it seems that &quot;one World of Darkness&quot; is turning into an ever changing construct... not sure if I like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 01-14-2016, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T00:21:03-08:00","id":808499,"title":"","content":"Truly it's shocking for me what they plan for werewolf storyline, here's my top 10 most jaw dropping changes:<br /> 1. Possibility of Gaia's death - described in Silver Fangs chapter.<br /> 2. Split of garou nation.<br /> 3 Almost complete change of Uktena tribe amd their camps including bitter and colder relations with Wendigo.<br /> 4. Return of Storm eater.<br /> 5. Entire Fianna tibe cursed.<br /> 6. Bone gnawers as common social class, not the homeless poor one.<br /> 7. Red talons growing in strength (I love the idea). And of course Impegrium.<br /> 8. Caern shards? and fall of greatest caerns.<br /> 9. Death of king Albrecht.<br /> 10. Black furies - it will be almost completely different tribe.<br /> <br /> Some of my friends/players are excided , some (Black fury player) are sceptical. I'm just waiting for full book and for more info's from White wolf. I don't like that they are quite silent about possible dates of release 4th ed games. Not everyone have enough money to travel to larp events. Sadly. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T01:20:23-08:00","id":808511,"title":"","content":"Uh. What? Are they trying to make a Werewolf LARP, or a whole new game?<br /> Maybe they are just formalising stuff that they feel works better in LARP then in tabletop?<br /> <br /> And if Ericsson is involved are we sure that this is about the WoD to come, and not just about his LARP projects?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T01:28:26-08:00","id":808514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=808495#post808495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what I've read from the Gamma slice it seems that &quot;one World of Darkness&quot; is turning into an ever changing construct... not sure if I like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do we have confirmation that this is actually a &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; product, though?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T01:39:57-08:00","id":808518,"title":"","content":"If you search youtube for the Tenebrae Noctis Videos you will hear him say, that he worked closely with BNS on the book, and that it contains a lot of elements that are to come to the WoD IV products (while it itself isn't one, though).<br /> <br /> And to me it feels like a whole new game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T02:16:18-08:00","id":808530,"title":"","content":"If met book story is similar or the same as in upcoming 4th wod books, werewolf the apocalypse would be truly different game. I'm tied to old npc's and as it seems they will be dead - most of leaders like Margrave, Albrecht. Curiously looking at the quotes in every tribe description, some of them may still live (Golgol, Amy hundred voices). I'm going to play W20 and 4th ed but i will consider if 4th will be continuation of chronicle or different game with new pc's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T03:26:44-08:00","id":808553,"title":"","content":"Some of the stuff is good, I've always disliked Bone Gnawers as the homeless tribe. And more Red Talons sounds neat.<br /> <br /> But, despite it being made for LARPs, I do think the changes are taking away some very important elements of WtA. The Umbra, the old Caerns, some tribal changes,etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T03:51:45-08:00","id":808562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=808429#post808429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get where many of these changes are coming from too.<br /> Playing a Metis in a LARP doesn't necessarily come with much penalty considering the way a lot of LARPs are played, so why punish players for playing such characters? Sure the Mules are looked down upon as representations of breaking the Litany and being sterile, but warriors that are sterile due to their fighting in the battles aren't looked down upon and are instead given Renown for their Battle Scars.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm ok with getting rid of the stigma for the Metis, I just don't like the idea then of saying they are 2nd class citizens. I guess I'd just prefer them to go the whole way and make the remaining 5 not care that much. <br /> <br /> As for a bulk of the changes, I do see a lot of the plot changes as not a bad thing at all. It'd a continuation I'm curious about more of the details. The only things so far I don't like is:<br /> <br /> 1) Male Black Furies (it misses the point of the tribe, this is a much bigger deal then the Fianna having issues with the Fae or the Bone Gnawers being more the common man then homeless. For me this is more like the Red Talons accepting homids)<br /> 2) Russian Wendigo (if this means what I think it means, it just smacks too much of Dances With Wolves cliches that are so common it'd be nice to avoid.)<br /> 3) Rage (going to try it out, but it seems a bit more complicated. Maybe this is just an old dog new trick issue)<br /> 4) Merits to play Fera (I don't agree with spending freebies to play them)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T04:17:17-08:00","id":808570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=808562#post808562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Male Black Furies (it misses the point of the tribe, this is a much bigger deal then the Fianna having issues with the Fae or the Bone Gnawers being more the common man then homeless. For me this is more like the Red Talons accepting homids)</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here. Just because Black Furies fight against oppression, doesn't mean they are inclusive. That is Children of Gaia's thing. Black Furies protect the sacred feminity, in good and in bad. Even if its cliche, the whole man-hating and murdering aspect is still part of the tribe. <br /> <br /> Imagine a group of witches laying curses on first born sons of a lineage, protecting their sisters but sacrificing the men. And all of that being very much effective and frightening. That is the Furies as much as the fight against oppression. They aren't Children of Gaia, and people should remember that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=808562#post808562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Russian Wendigo (if this means what I think it means, it just smacks too much of Dances With Wolves cliches that are so common it'd be nice to avoid.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, first off, I doubt they are speaking of white russians. Instead, I think they mean the native people of siberia: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigenous_peoples_of_Siberia\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indige...les_of_Siberia</a><br /> <br /> And given how close Alaska is to Russia, I can see Wendigo seeking kin in Siberia.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T04:33:26-08:00","id":808576,"title":"","content":"I think the Fera through merits is a LARP thing. In general the fall of the Garou Nation and new alliances change the setting a lot and where Changing Breeds were their own thing in Werewolf now the whole world has a possibility of mixing garou and other fera, not just Hengeyokai and Ahadi.<br /> This is partly due to the fact, that if you have 30+ players there are always some who want to be even more special than everyone else and that often is a Corax, Nuwisha or Bastet character for those players. Personally I go by &quot;We play Werewolf, not were-whatever&quot; but I can see how White Wolf and BNS want to include them in regular games and be done with the discussion.<br /> <br /> So, in the interest of equally build characters the fera are merits, just as Rank seems to be a background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T04:46:25-08:00","id":808581,"title":"","content":"<br /> It's very good rule. I made ma mistake some time ago and agreed to put khan pc character in campaign. From that time WtA is werewolf only game. Player playing weretiger annoyed everyone including me (and i am very patient man),he played to destroy session so he's tiger ended up as a football ball used by Get.<br /> Mixing fera with werewolf packs isn't my favourite thing I simply prefer garou victory in War of rage and animosity between them and fera rather then cooperation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T06:19:28-08:00","id":808615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=808570#post808570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, first off, I doubt they are speaking of white russians. Instead, I think they mean the native people of siberia: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigenous_peoples_of_Siberia\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indige...les_of_Siberia</a><br /> <br /> And given how close Alaska is to Russia, I can see Wendigo seeking kin in Siberia.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably the Siberakh. But I would have rather introduced the SIberakh, then just merged them with Wendigo.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T07:10:45-08:00","id":808660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=808351#post808351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> O.o ....o.O<br /> <br /> Uh, anyone LARPing, is this a thing there? Because it sounds very silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's one way that GMs limit the presence of Fera in convention games where you simply cannot vet every player but also want to accomodate every player.<br /> <br /> Org games (MES and OWBN) have approval systems in place.<br /> <br /> A lot of the <i>mechanical</i> changes bring MET:WTA more in line with MET:VTM, but I just can't imagine <i>anyone</i> wanting these sweeping setting changes introduced through the LARP book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T08:01:19-08:00","id":808703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=808570#post808570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, first off, I doubt they are speaking of white russians. Instead, I think they mean the native people of siberia: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigenous_peoples_of_Siberia\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indige...les_of_Siberia</a><br /> <br /> And given how close Alaska is to Russia, I can see Wendigo seeking kin in Siberia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, which if that's the case I'm ok with it. However it said both Siberian and Russian. Since they stated both I read the Russian part as meaning white.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T09:12:08-08:00","id":808756,"title":"","content":"Check out the KickStarter updates. They've posted how they make changes based on the player feedback.<br /> <br /> I'm curious with the move of 4th Edition created in-house at Paradox Interactive, if the usual Gen Con release may change to something European? Normally I'd say &quot;watch for something at Gen Con&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which makes me wonder if OPP will share a booth with PI this year?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:40:58-08:00","id":809043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=808660#post808660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's one way that GMs limit the presence of Fera in convention games where you simply cannot vet every player but also want to accomodate every player.<br /> <br /> Org games (MES and OWBN) have approval systems in place.<br /> <br /> A lot of the <i>mechanical</i> changes bring MET:WTA more in line with MET:VTM, but I just can't imagine <i>anyone</i> wanting these sweeping setting changes introduced through the LARP book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's also tied into a concept they call the <a href=\"http://www.bynightstudios.com/the-economy-of-cool-from-st-secrets/\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;economy of cool.&quot;</a> The idea is that, while they want people to be able to play unusual things as the setting allows, they also want to make sure that people aren't dominating the scene with too many cool things. Rarer types of Changing Breeds cost merit points to prevent people from playing the strange thing AND getting a full load of other cool things through as well, thus edging out the person playing a &quot;regular&quot; concept (i.e. Garou) with those same &quot;cool&quot; merits. In Africa, werecats are just uncommon, and thus don't cost as much because it's more likely to see them, and they're not as special. It also encourages people to play the more standard and common character types, since those characters have more freedom to them, and presents a trade-off between relatively unusual powers and having more flexibility.<br /> <br /> It also acts as a useful tool for organized games, since they can alter the rarity levels. In the MES, where we use the BNS rules for Vampire in two games (one for Camarilla, Anarchs, and Independents, and the other for the Sabbat), there are two different rarity sets for the two different settings, to reflect the &quot;unusualness&quot; of a particular concept in each one - where the Crusader bloodline has a point cost in the core book and the Cam/Anarch venue, it's the default in the Sabbat venue and doesn't cost any XP. This allows the game runners to tailor the game setting to fit their expectations and personal story.<br /> <br /> If you're doing a home game, on the other hand, and you don't like rarity merits, you can choose to get rid of them or alter how the cost is paid. I'm in a Dark Ages Vampire game run off of BNS - none of the base clans are any rarer than any other (except for the Daughters and the Gargoyles, who are off limits), and playing a Bloodline costs XP, but NOT Merit slots (so, you can pay the points to belong to the True Brujah Bloodline, but still have seven points worth of general or clan-specific merits). There's still a cost, but it comes from the starting XP pool, not from the options you can use merits for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1407,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","user":"EndlessKng","date":".  changed the term and added in a link to the article in question 01-15-2016, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T14:46:09-08:00","id":810823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=808660#post808660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of the <i>mechanical</i> changes bring MET:WTA more in line with MET:VTM, but I just can't imagine <i>anyone</i> wanting these sweeping setting changes introduced through the LARP book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I personally find it unfortunate, too.<br /> <br /> If there was a clear statement &quot;This is already a pre-view of what the Setting will look like in 4th Edition&quot; and if there was a &quot;4th Edition&quot; logo or something on the book, it would be a lot clearer, that this is a new(er) Setting.<br /> <br /> Shadowrun and several other games managed to brand their 4th, 5th and so on editions and it was clear, what books belonged to what edition. This wasn't the case with revised and 2nd Edition. It is kind of the case with x20 books and supplements.<br /> I hope it will be the case for all tabletop books at least.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T14:52:23-08:00","id":810825,"title":"","content":"So for the record I did e-mail my opinions to BNS, even though I have not put money into the KS. Currently as the product stands, I am not planning on funding this KS. Some of the setting changes just aren't my thing. Its not that I don't like the entire thing, its just some of the changes just really aren't for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T21:22:09-08:00","id":810954,"title":"","content":"Probably let that also be known to Martin at White Wolf...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T22:19:43-08:00","id":810968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=810954#post810954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably let that also be known to Martin at White Wolf...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not sure how to do that, or I would if it would mean anything. Again its not that I hate the entire thing there are just a few sticking points for me. I've been a long time White Wolf fan since I first started playing Rage back in '95. It'd be weird for me to see the games go off in a direction that I just can't identify with anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T22:21:04-08:00","id":810969,"title":"","content":"Odd part is I'm not even a Black Fury Fanboy yet their change is one of the things that feels so big to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-17T23:39:53-08:00","id":810995,"title":"","content":"There is an info eMail address at the white wolf homepage.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of people feel like you do. For me it is not that the changes are too big, it is that they come and it is still W:tA. Marvel and DC make big changes every ten years, but they at least brand their universes differently, like Marvel Now, New 52 and so on.<br /> <br /> In general I don't like world changing events at all. Not that there should be stagnation, but I can't see that there were any &quot;world changing&quot; events in the last 10 or even 20 years that warrant such a huge change in the WoD (which is essentially supposed to mirror the real world).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T07:23:40-08:00","id":811097,"title":"","content":"For me, it just feels like they wanted to make Furies more accepting, not understanding the point of the tribe or its culture. The Children of Gaia are all ready the accepting tribe, no need to make the Furies as such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T07:34:21-08:00","id":811105,"title":"","content":"I think there is a distinct difference in the approach the tribes have. But it also seems the Garou Nation has shattered and Children of Gaia are amongst the pro-Weaver-alliance faction, while the Black Furies probably are not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-18T09:23:40-08:00","id":811159,"title":"","content":"Well, my intent of this post was mostly to also encourage folks to pledge for pins that have never before been available, even if you don't plan to get the PDF. :-) <br /> <br /> The more folks can pledge early, the faster we'll reach those goals you want! You can always change your pledge before the end of the KickStarter, so if you're waiting now because you're waiting for your pin/group to unlock, you're really only hurting yourself and others in the same boat. :-/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.co