./posts/1473977</a><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T08:06:15-08:00","id":816890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=816490#post816490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HEY! Yeah, you!<br /> By Night Studios has made a change in direction (as far as the KickStarter's stretch goals and pins are concerned) and they've <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>UNLOCKED AUSPICE PINS EARLY!</b></span></span> Right from the start, you're guaranteed to be able to get all five pins! Does that pique your interest? Help us fund ALL of the pins, if not the book and additional content as well!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is orthogonal to the change in direction I'm hoping to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T09:05:44-08:00","id":818480,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Here's the email I just sent to </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection\" class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"f990979f96b98e91908d9c8e96959fd4898c9b95908a9190979ed79a9694\">[email&#160;protected]</a> re: </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/bynightstudios/minds-eye-theatre-werewolf-the-apocalypse/posts/1475845</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just read the latest update to BNS' MET:WTA Kickstarter and it is clear their vision for WTA involves sweeping changes to the setting that render it incompatible with how the game is played in the present and how I intend to play the game in the future. On their campaign page, they say &quot;we are thrilled to be working with them [Paradox Interactive] directly on key elements of the story and metaplot for this book.&quot; If that is the case, I have no intention of buying your World of Darkness books, either. These changes in the settings that they propose are more drastic, more extreme, more difficult for GMs to reconcile than any of the changes White Wolf made in their original run of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hate being a grognard.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T10:48:52-08:00","id":818572,"title":"","content":"Hopefully this will prompt them to keep their LARP line separate from their Table Top then (I have a feeling its too late for LARP)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T10:49:56-08:00","id":818575,"title":"","content":"I wrote to BNS, maybe I'll write a white wolf e-mail too so you're not the only voice. As it stands I've bought every WtA book that OP has put out, but refuse to back BNS currently due to those changes I've already voiced to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T13:49:53-08:00","id":818703,"title":"","content":"I don't know, maybe Disney killing all of the Star Wars EU made me jaded, but I don't really care what they do to Werewolf the Apocalypse, going forward. I still have my old books and stories. If the new material has good ideas I will happily pillage them, and if the new stuff is stupid I will ignore it and carry on. I am going to reserve my judgement for a later date.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T17:31:48-08:00","id":818867,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The KickStarter is officially funded now</b>. </span> Now it's time to unlock the rest of the pins!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/bynightstudios/minds-eye-theatre-werewolf-the-apocalypse/posts/1473977\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/1473977</a><br /> <br /> As for the setting, to be honest, I don't mind the shake-up in the setting--I've played in far worse settings in Werewolf games.<br /> I don't mind the two new camps (Concordat of the Stars and Sanctum of Gaia.) I don't mind a setting where Garou have a much harder time at things and must find new ways of dealing with this enemy in a time that truly feels like it's in The Age of the Apocalypse, rather than skirting just before it. It feels much more desperate with a real need to fight, or die. But since the Setting info is still being worked on and hasn't really been released in full yet, I still have many questions and not as many answers as I'd like.<br /> But, then, if I'm not a fan of the final setting, I still have W20 to use for our tabletop games (Hell, I could still play 1st Edition before everything turned into Carebears-with-claws land.)<br /> <br /> But again, they're producing these with the blessing and help of the Lead Storyline developer at the new White Wolf Publishing. IF you want to talk to White Wolf in-person, they'll be at a few conventions this year and you can talk to them about their 4th Edition setting. March 9 - 14th 2016. The Baltic Sea. <a href=\"http://www.solmukohta.org/\" target=\"_blank\">Solmukohta</a>.<br /> May 19 - 22nd 2016. Austin. <a href=\"http://www.livinggamesconference.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Living Games</a>.<br /> September, 2016. New Orleans. <a href=\"http://www.masqueradebynight.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Grand Masquerade</a>.<br /> @etherial<br /> Unfortunately, your Email isn't very helpful, or constructive. You don't have any examples of what items in the book/setting you take issue with and how they differ from the play styles you use.<br /> You need to use specifics, referencing and offering constructive critique and suggestions if you want your comments to have a chance of having any influence.<br /> <br /> I would suggest the same thing for anyone else with concerns, or suggestions too. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T20:16:12-08:00","id":818951,"title":"","content":"I've got beef with BNS over their Vampire stuff but all of these Werewolf changes are fine by me. Don't really see the issues here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T03:00:50-08:00","id":819076,"title":"","content":"Well, the game setting changed a lot.<br /> And I for one hope that they have a &quot;Age of Apocalypse&quot; logo, or &quot;IV Edition&quot; logo to mark all books as belonging to a new edition and don't write the new descriptions as if the world/the tribes/ the whatever had been that way, but go the extra mile and check that changes are evident as such and marked as recent developments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T04:42:14-08:00","id":819110,"title":"","content":"The Garou nation splits into.. One side that is objectively Wrong(&quot;Double Down on shit that doesn't work!&quot;) and one side that lets you play with Fera as Gaia intended! Seriously with how crossover happy I've generally seen Werewolf larps(&quot;you mages can come help, and you too fera&quot;) the break in the garou nation seems like &quot;ok these tribes are npcs now!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T04:46:23-08:00","id":819112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=818951#post818951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've got beef with BNS over their Vampire stuff but all of these Werewolf changes are fine by me. Don't really see the issues here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm glad for you. You and the funding that arrived to BNS prove that there are people interested in that. These products will be made and you will get to enjoy them. It doesn't mean that everyone wants something like that, though. I can tell you that my reaction to this is about as bad as yours to the Vampire souls thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T05:06:45-08:00","id":819127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=819112#post819112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I'm glad for you. You and the funding that arrived to BNS prove that there are people interested in that. These products will be made and you will get to enjoy them. It doesn't mean that everyone wants something like that, though. I can tell you that my reaction to this is about as bad as yours to the Vampire souls thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say you are on the larger side of the group, Compare how long it took to fund BNS werewolf with Werwolf 20","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T05:36:46-08:00","id":819143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=819112#post819112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'm glad for you. You and the funding that arrived to BNS prove that there are people interested in that. These products will be made and you will get to enjoy them. It doesn't mean that everyone wants something like that, though. I can tell you that my reaction to this is about as bad as yours to the Vampire souls thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the funding off W20 showed that there are people who want the nostalgia products, too.<br /> <br /> I think we can't know for a long time, how well received the changes Martin brings to the WoD will be.<br /> I, generally, like a Setting that has a Status Quo and that isn't changing constantly. If I talk to people about WtA, I don't want to specify Edition or fictional timelines to punctuate the scope of the discussion. With SR it so okay, since the Edition is in the title, so I'd like something like that for the new WoD, too.<br /> <br /> For, really, the WoD Martins seems to present is a continuation of the WoD, but it is as much a new world as ST:TOS is different from ST:TNG or Shadowrun3 is from Shadowrun4 or SR5, or Deadlands:Weird West is different from Deadlands: Hell on earth.<br /> <br /> So, that is what I wish for, going forward: Make this &quot;Werewolf: Age of Apocalypse&quot; or &quot;WtA IV&quot; as a setting, and generate a logo for it, so it is distinguishable.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T06:11:23-08:00","id":819161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=818867#post818867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately, your Email isn't very helpful, or constructive. You don't have any examples of what items in the book/setting you take issue with and how they differ from the play styles you use.<br /> You need to use specifics, referencing and offering constructive critique and suggestions if you want your comments to have a chance of having any influence.<br /> <br /> I would suggest the same thing for anyone else with concerns, or suggestions too.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very good point. Perhaps if I move back to Bargaining from Depression I'll send them a more detailed letter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T07:41:10-08:00","id":819236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I've got beef with BNS over their Vampire stuff but all of these Werewolf changes are fine by me. Don't really see the issues here.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Imagine if Kindred were noted as being born that way from time to time like in Blade, or if there was some bizarre, tortured explanation to try and justify why being a vampire has anything to do with a character's DNA. This is just one issue that cropped up in the Alpha slice's Silver Fangs writeup, mentioning biting kin to change their DNA.<br /> <br /> Revised did away with the Garou gene concept back in 1999. The Beta Slice's writeup of the Get of Fenris sounded suspiciously like it ignored the Revised tribebook, too.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, so many tribes jumping ship to the Weaver from out of nowhere has merged with The Laughing One's Star Wars reference, making me expect these tribes to start ranting about how <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2tLf1JO5bvE\" target=\"_blank\">they don't like dirt.</a></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=819143#post819143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the funding off W20 showed that there are people who want the nostalgia products, too.<br /> <br /> I think we can't know for a long time, how well received the changes Martin brings to the WoD will be.<br /> I, generally, like a Setting that has a Status Quo and that isn't changing constantly. If I talk to people about WtA, I don't want to specify Edition or fictional timelines to punctuate the scope of the discussion. With SR it so okay, since the Edition is in the title, so I'd like something like that for the new WoD, too.<br /> <br /> For, really, the WoD Martins seems to present is a continuation of the WoD, but it is as much a new world as ST:TOS is different from ST:TNG or Shadowrun3 is from Shadowrun4 or SR5, or Deadlands:Weird West is different from Deadlands: Hell on earth.<br /> <br /> So, that is what I wish for, going forward: Make this &quot;Werewolf: Age of Apocalypse&quot; or &quot;WtA IV&quot; as a setting, and generate a logo for it, so it is distinguishable.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And if they were going to do a new world, they could have at least moved some things around a bit more, like not have so many tribes centered in Europe for so long. There was really no need to retcon much of that in with some bizarre &quot;heritage reset&quot; after Anthelios showed up and then disappeared. Werewolf has a history of not bothering to explain why changes happened, unlike in Vampire; again, Get of Fenris Revised. It completely up-ended everything people though that they might have known about the tribe, particularly from the previous splatbook about it, but didn't mention any events happening to make it go through. It was a hard revision of lore that assumed it was the way things had always been, much like the lack of need for mirrors to step sideways, changed from the need for one before Revised. What didn't work got junked backwards in time, never to plague the game again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T19:35:59-08:00","id":819642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=819127#post819127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Compare how long it took to fund BNS werewolf with Werwolf 20</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not a good comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T23:53:02-08:00","id":819715,"title":"","content":"Agreed. Comparing W20 to BNS isn't really apples to apples.<br /> BNS:MET:V:tM took 10 days to reach $70K. BNS:MET:W:tA took 15.<br /> I think the issue here is that the LARP community is much smaller than the TT community too.<br /> Also, the KickStarter for the Vampire book included more high-end tiers, and the primary Clan pins available right off the bat.<br /> <br /> As for the setting, as far as I can tell, everything up until &quot;<a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/1619/Apocalypse\" target=\"_blank\">APOCALYPSE</a>&quot; is still canon (or as canon as Werewolf can/has been considering they've changed mechanics and some setting material between editions before too.) It's just that everything after the book of potential endings had lead to 2016, and the world they've unveiled for us. The Age of Apocalypse has begun, and the game starts in the middle of it... is it the very end, or is it the darkest hour before the dawn? The first new Caern in 15 years has been created, and suddenly Garou have discovered that some Kinfolk can be turned into Garou too. Obviously there have been great metaphysical changes in the world, but you might expect that as the Apocalypse starts to crank it up to 11.<br /> <br /> And I haven't read yet that the whole Nation has split into two; there are just two new camps that you can join if you'd like (Concordate of the stars, and the Sanctum of Gaia). I don't think you could be a Santcum of Gaia and a Judge of Doom at the same time, because I don't think you can be part of two camps at once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T00:11:38-08:00","id":819720,"title":"","content":"Oh, and the Silver Fangs pin is now locked-in!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-31T23:46:46-08:00","id":820783,"title":"","content":"I agree with your analysis, Torakhan. But, the question is, if people want or need big metaphysical changes, or even an Apocalypse?<br /> <br /> The book of the ToJ-line was presenting scenarios and you weren't required to run them, the world could still go on as before, even today in 2016. Our LARP game did. And we would be perfectly happy with a total overhaul for the tabletop game mechanics, getting rid of some design flaws and maybe bring in some stuff that worked well in nWoD or Exalted. Or maybe do something completely new (I always liked percentage systems with no experience points like early RuneQuest),<br /> <br /> But as for the Setting, there is no real need for change. Forcing a global spiritual disaster and culture changing events from 2004 to 2016 into the game seems like a bad choice...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T00:30:39-08:00","id":820807,"title":"","content":"Well its definitely something....I don't think its WtA though, seems like someones homebrew local setting. Luckily I don't LARP these days so I get to avoid the entire situation....I have a feeling the majority of old school Werewolf LARPs here are going to be a no-sell on the changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T08:59:14-08:00","id":821029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=820807#post820807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well its definitely something....I don't think its WtA though, seems like someones homebrew local setting. Luckily I don't LARP these days so I get to avoid the entire situation....I have a feeling the majority of old school Werewolf LARPs here are going to be a no-sell on the changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't know how large the group is, that would or would not incorporate such changes into their chronicles. But I think that Martin has cooperated with the BNS people to bring glimpses of what he wants the WoD to be into the book. And so, the changes will be in tabletop games too, within two or three years, probably.<br /> Why do I think White Wolf will go this way?<br /> Because Martin said so on a panel at a White Wolf convention in Germany last December.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T19:16:49-08:00","id":825198,"title":"","content":"Posting to report that the Shadow Lords pin recently got unlocked. <a href=\"http://werewolf-news.com/\" target=\"_blank\">And the KS got covered by Werewolf-news.com on Feb. 5th.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T21:19:04-08:00","id":825754,"title":"","content":"So I've been browsing the gamma slice so far and there are definitely parts I don't care for and from what I've read I'm not alone. First thing, the Garou Nation didn't really need to split as the whole thing with Apocalypse is that the Nation was just beginning to realize that they'd all lose if they didn't at least try to work together in the end. It wasn't a huggy, friendly kind of cooperation but their backs were up against the wall and it was a &quot;do or die&quot; situation. It also seems like the Tribes as a whole have actually taken a huge step back in their outlooks. The Revised TB for the Get had them not particularly caring if you were Metis, sure they were on a lower level by the nature of their births but if a Metis could prove themselves in battle then they were accepted. They also seemed to retcon them back into being racists who are starting to realize that racism is bad. The Get were presented in valuing strength and as of Revised they didn't care so much about skin color as a measure of value.<br /> <br /> Then they actually made the Red Talons worse, which isn't something I thought possible. The Impergium will never be a thing again and while the Talons have always been calling for a return to it, now they're actually going through with it and Lupus of other tribes think it's a good idea and might be looking to join in? Not in this day and age. If the Garou are dumb enough to try that again they'd honestly deserve extinction at the hands of humanity.<br /> <br /> Male Black Furies? Screw that. I get that they're trying to make the tribe more inclusive or attractive to the player base but it goes against the very nature of the tribe. It's not inclusive or progressive or making a statement, it's actually a step back in my eyes and makes the tribe into the status quo. Women are half the global population and yet considered a minority, men are in the vast majority of positions of power (yeah I know the book says males can't rise above 3rd rank), and what I think the ultimate result that this change will make in the game is that there will be more male Black Furies than female if we're looking at the demographics of the hobby being any indication. Once again, I think it's majorly missing the point of the tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T21:36:56-08:00","id":825756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/804780-bns-kickstarter-for-met-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=821029#post821029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I don't know how large the group is, that would or would not incorporate such changes into their chronicles. But I think that Martin has cooperated with the BNS people to bring glimpses of what he wants the WoD to be into the book. And so, the changes will be in tabletop games too, within two or three years, probably.<br /> Why do I think White Wolf will go this way?<br /> Because Martin said so on a panel at a White Wolf convention in Germany last December.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd be surprised if Werewolf is out in 2 to 3 years maybe 3 to 4 range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T04:08:41-08:00","id":825913,"title":"","content":"All these changes to the setting reminds me of why I don't like metaplot in my WoD<br /> <br /> \u200bOh well, I'll be sticking to W20 and 1e for my tabletop needs and Laws of the Wild for my LARP needs. I knew BNS likes to continue the metaplot but I wondered if it was possible to keep the mechanics and remove the metaplot (similar to how I do with Revised Edition MET books) but it seems the changes are so drastic that it won't be possible.<br /> <br /> Either way, I'm going to pass this up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T05:00:33-08:00","id":825922,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I too think, that for tabletop and maybe LARP, there is a group of people who would like a more static Setting, without drastic changes, however with updated rules and mechanics that removes some of the minor flaws of the game, without completely out-dating everything you knew about the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T01:12:29-08:00","id":836915,"title":"","content":"12 years is a long time. Stuff should've happened in that time. BNS MET effectively is a new edition, as we already had the Revised LARP stuff. The BNS tag already does differentiate it from previous editions. So that's not really the issue. The issue is that you don't like the changes, which is fine but also totally subjective.<br /> <br /> If you want Martin to consider why certain changes won't suit many players, then you need to point out which ones, why, and how many people are against the changes. Otherwise, it's hard to take your email as anything other than an old player who doesn't like change, and there will always be those players with every new edition.<br /> <br /> I'd recommend that anyone who doesn't like the changes say so on the KS and send in an email being specific. There has to be a sense that there's widespread dissatisfaction with the changes before they become serious enough to consider.<br /> <br /> Honestly, though, from what I read of the interview with Martin, it looks like he has his own ideas and isn't particularly interested in other people's ideas. His comments about Revised Edition and later material, for example, do seem a little contemptuous of other perspectives on how the game should be played. I'm hoping, though, that he's mostly hands off when it comes to TT and that it's LARP and the online game that he's mostly interested in.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that future products may change a lot because Martin isn't really targeting us as buyers any more. If TT is to become a secondary product to a WoD MMORPG, the focus might shift towards new players (thus widening the market) rather than old players (thus catering to a slowly shrinking market as we old-timers drop off).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T02:12:28-08:00","id":836934,"title":"","content":"Sure, stuff should have happened. But an entire civilization of supernatural beings changed more or less radical?<br /> It's a matter of opinion. I mean what has happened for humanity or at least most of humanity. The change from flap-phone to smartphone didn't bring a huge cultural cataclysm. Neither did the change from George W. to Barack. Sure, there were events that changed the world (more or less) like arab spring, but how did they affect the live of people in other regions and how much lasting effect did they have for the people really affected?<br /> <br /> I would be totally fine with 12 years of garou going out fighting the Wyrm and do so again the next day.<br /> <br /> <br /> That said, I'm pretty sure Martin and Tobias want a unified WoD over many media and so tabletop will see all the changes, too, and more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-27T21:18:20-08:00","id":838442,"title":"","content":"So far <b>Ahroun</b>, <b>Galliard</b>, <b>Philodox</b>, <b>Theurge</b>, <b>Ragabash</b>, <b>Silver Fangs</b>, <b>Shadow Lords</b>, <b>Get of Fenris</b>, <b>Glass Walkers</b>, <b>Bone Gnawers</b>, and <b>Fianna</b> pins have been unlocked!<br /> <br /> 2 days left to pledge!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/bynightstudios/minds-eye-theatre-werewolf-the-apocalypse/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...he-apocalypse/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\"